{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "experiment": {
    "name": "ibm_cal_heuristic_floor",
    "description": "The label-free floor under the calendar-forward regime. Calendar-forward regime: every entity with history is scored at fixed origins (train 2022-09-05, validation 2022-09-07, test 2022-09-09) from transactions before the origin; label = involvement in a flagged transaction in [origin, origin + 2 days).",
    "tags": [
      "unsupervised",
      "calendar-forward",
      "ibm"
    ],
    "seed": 42,
    "dataset": {
      "name": "ibm_aml_hi_small",
      "version": "size475664283-c9a6aae1",
      "provenance": "file:C:\\Users\\bhara\\Downloads\\Laundering Data\\HI-Small_Trans.csv",
      "label_definition": "positive = the (bank, account) entity is the payer or the payee of at least one transaction whose published 'Is Laundering' flag is 1. IBM labels transactions; this entity label is derived, and it makes a launderer's counterparty positive as well",
      "synthetic": true,
      "notes": [
        "SYNTHETIC: IBM AMLworld virtual-world simulator (Altman et al., NeurIPS 2023 Datasets and Benchmarks). Not evidence about real-world detection.",
        "Entity is the (bank, account) pair; account strings are not globally unique (8 collisions across banks).",
        "Amounts are native across 15 currencies (37% USD) and are not FX-converted; the amount column is 'amount', not 'amount_usd'.",
        "The typology names live in the separate HI-Small_Patterns.txt and are deliberately not loaded: their group headers state the generating mechanism and its degree/hop parameter.",
        "Version is derived from file size and mtime, not a content hash; the content hash is in data/manifests/ibm_aml_hi_small.json."
      ]
    },
    "features": {
      "sets": [
        "aml_txn_v1",
        "aml_temporal_v1",
        "aml_flow_v1",
        "aml_context_v1",
        "aml_network_v1",
